<title>USA: Australia's News Corp ADRs rise.</title>
<headline>Australia's News Corp ADRs rise.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's News Corp Ltd rose in heavy volume Thursday to highlight trade in American Depositary Receipts  ADRs.</p>
<p>Ordinary ADRs rose 1/2 to 18-1/2 after News Corp signed two deals worth a total of almost $3 billion. It will sell its American Sky Broadcasting satellite assets to Primestar Partner LP in exchange for equity and buy cable network International Family Entertainment.</p>
<p>Volume was 1.4 million shares in late afternoon, almost three times normal daily trade, and the ADRs were the most active on New York exchanges.</p>
<p>Among other active shares, Brazilian telephone company Telebras SA rose 2-3/4 to 139-5/8 and Britain's Danka Business Systems Plc was up 2-3/8 to 43-1/8.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk (212) 859-1730))</p>
